  "body": "The #919 research found 10 files in `crates/app/tests` that import nothing `app` defines (8 belong to post, `boundary_walls` to sim, `arcs` to motion) and 2 misplaced files in `crates/motion/tests` (`real_tip` -> sim, `origin_approach` -> cl). Move them; no new dependency between crates, no seam work.\n\nSafety: these are pinning tests - the `#[test]` count per file must be the same before and after, and every moved test must still run in the batch tier (check `xtask/src/plan.rs` picks them up in their new crate).\n\nDone means: the 12 files compile in their owner crate with no `camcraft_app` import; their Gate maps name the real crate; the test count is unchanged; the quick tier selects them for a change in their own crate.\n\nLists, counts and evidence: the research comment on #919 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-6808141599).\n\nPart of #919.\n",
